        "projectInstructionsLoaded": [],
        "finalMessage": "I fixed both issues in `collapsible.tsx`, but I couldn't re-lint it: the project has no installed `node_modules`, and the command to check for a global oxlint or ultracite needed approval. So the fix hasn't been checked by the linter.\n\n**The problem:** the header row in `Collapsible` was a plain `<div>` that toggled the section on click. Keyboard and screen-reader users couldn't reach or use it.\n\n**The change (line 122):** I gave the `<div>` the behaviour of a real button:\n- `role=\"button\"` so it's announced as a button. This clears `no-static-element-interactions`.\n- `tabIndex={0}` so you can Tab to it.\n- An `onKeyDown` handler that calls `openTrigger()` on Enter or Space. It also stops Space from scrolling the page. This clears `click-events-have-key-events`.\n- `aria-expanded={open}` so screen readers say whether the section is open. The rules didn't require this, but a collapsible header needs it.\n\nClick behaviour, styling and layout are unchanged.\n\n**Why not use a `<button>` element:** the header's `label` is an `<h3>` (per `Stats/index.tsx`), and a heading isn't allowed inside a `<button>`. A `<button>` would also bring default browser styles that change how the header looks.\n\n**Possible new warning:** Ultracite's config might enable a rule that prefers native elements over ARIA roles (`jsx-a11y/prefer-tag-over-role`). I couldn't confirm whether it's on. If it is, it will flag `role=\"button\"`. Clearing it would mean switching to a `<button>` and restructuring the `<h3>` label, which is a design decision for a person to make.",
        "styleMentions": [
