        "finalMessage": "I replaced the `<div role=\"button\">` in `collapsible.tsx` with a real `<button type=\"button\">`, so the `prefer-tag-over-role` rule shouldn't apply any more. I couldn't confirm that, though: both attempts to run oxlint were blocked for approval, so the file hasn't been re-linted.\n\n- **Removed what the native button already provides:** I took out `role=\"button\"`, `tabIndex={0}` and the `onKeyDown` handler. A real button is focusable and already fires `onClick` on Enter and Space, so `openTrigger` still runs the same way. `aria-expanded`, `className` and `onClick` are unchanged.\n- **Kept the original look:** I added inline style resets so the button still looks like the old full-width header row. These set `background` and `border` to none, `margin` and `padding` to 0, `font`, `color` and `textAlign` to inherit, and `width: \"100%\"`. The original `display: flex`, `alignItems`, `justifyContent` and `cursor` are still there.\n\nThe label passed in from Stats is an `<h3>`, and strict HTML doesn't allow a heading inside a `<button>`. Browsers render it fine. Screen readers lose the heading role here, but that already happened with the old `role=\"button\"`, so this is no worse than before. To keep the heading for screen readers, the caller would put the button inside the `<h3>` rather than the other way round. That means changing `Stats/index.tsx`, which is outside this task, so I left it.",
